From 85298241f2ca781cdd6c411f0c9da90656ad22c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:00:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Real ring 3 user processes: fix scheduler/context switch, add
 validated syscalls

Bugs fixed:
- switch_context read its arguments from eax/edx, but i386 cdecl passes them
  on the stack; it also had the fabricated stack frame in the wrong pop order.
- user_entry used the *kernel* ESP as the user stack pointer and never mapped a
  user stack.
- USER_BASE (16 MiB) overlapped the kernel identity map; PDE U/S bit was not
  set when a user page landed in an existing page table.
- Nothing ever called create_process(); no user process could run.
- A fault in ring 3 halted the whole machine (only #PF was survivable).
- ISR stub left user data selectors loaded in kernel mode.
- Syscalls dereferenced raw user pointers (kernel memory read/write primitive).
- yield() could switch to a blocked idle task; per-process CR3 was never
  restored for the idle/shell task; zombies leaked their address space.

Added:
- user/ runtime + linker script, built-in programs embedded via userprog.S
- uaccess.c: user_range_ok()/user_strncpy(); vmm_check_user(),
  vmm_destroy_address_space()
- process_wait()/reaping, sleep/wake, user-mode-only timer preemption
- shell: run <prog> [&], progs, usertest; make test-user
